@* A link as it is printed: its QR code, its words and its address written short. The code is the link, so a PDF
   read on a screen can still be clicked. Drawn on paper only: its style hides it on a screen. *@
<a class="@Class" href="@Href" target="@Target" rel="@Rel">
    <QrImage Value="@Whole" Label="@($"QR code: {Label}")"/>
    <span class="paper-link-words"><b>@Label</b><span class="paper-link-address">@Written</span></span>
</a>
